BraleModule_Validate
├── when amount is zero
│   └── it should return false with "Zero amount"
├── when params are shorter than 96 bytes
│   └── it should return false with "Invalid params encoding"
├── when params use the old two-field encoding
│   └── it should return false with "Invalid params encoding"
├── when params have dirty address bits
│   └── it should return false with "Invalid params encoding"
├── when depositAddress is zero
│   └── it should return false with "Zero deposit address"
├── when depositAddress is the PaymentRails
│   └── it should return false with "Deposit address is PaymentRails"
├── when depositAddress is the module
│   └── it should return false with "Deposit address is module"
├── when depositAddress is the input token
│   └── it should return false with "Deposit address is input token"
├── when depositAddress is the output token
│   └── it should return false with "Deposit address is output token"
├── when outputToken is zero
│   └── it should return false with "Zero output token"
├── when outputToken equals the input token
│   └── it should return false with "Output token equals input token"
├── when minAmount is zero
│   └── it should return false with "Zero minimum amount"
├── when amount is below minAmount
│   └── it should return false with "Below minimum redemption"
├── when amount equals minAmount
│   └── it should return true
└── when params are valid
    ├── it should return true with an empty reason
    ├── it should not check the PaymentRails balance
    └── it should be callable by any address
